WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Why does a feather feel smooth one way and rough the other?

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.200
Fish scales can feel that way, too.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.220
At the kitchen table, your child can compare animal coverings and use what they

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.360
notice to sort pictures.

5
00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:19.633
This activity lets your child practice looking closely and describing what they

6
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:25.573
actually feel. They make a guess, test it with water, and sort animal pictures by

7
00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:26.633
rules they explain.

8
00:00:28.093 --> 00:00:30.813
Formal group names like mammal or reptile can wait.

9
00:00:31.867 --> 00:00:36.747
Set out three to five craft-store feathers, fake fur, and two or three clean shells.

10
00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:39.867
Add a cup of water and a dropper.

11
00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:44.967
If you use raw fish, choose a piece with skin and scales still attached.

12
00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:47.287
Put it on a plate.

13
00:00:48.427 --> 00:00:51.527
Keep twelve to sixteen animal pictures face down nearby.

14
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.080
Stay with your child.

15
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.000
Handle raw fish, scissors, and glass magnifiers yourself.

16
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.700
Check shells for sharp edges.

17
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.540
Use only craft-store feathers.

18
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.100
Leave wild feathers where you find them.

19
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.640
Keep small shells, small feathers, and loose dropper parts from children under four.

20
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.380
Call nine one one if choking.

21
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.660
Use photos if anyone is allergic to a material.

22
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:25.893
Have your child describe the feather, fur, and shell in two words each.

23
00:01:27.233 --> 00:01:28.973
Open and smooth the feather's edge.

24
00:01:30.273 --> 00:01:34.653
If you're using raw fish and have no cuts or sores on your hands, stroke it both

25
00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:38.433
ways. Keep hands away from faces and mouths.

26
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:44.633
Wash your hands with soap and water immediately after touching fish, before touching

27
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:45.633
anything else.

28
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.730
Before the water test, ask, "Which one will stay driest if it gets wet?"

29
00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.850
Place three drops on the feather and three on the fur.

30
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.010
Water often beads on feathers, while fur and craft feathers vary.

31
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.050
Each coat fits where an animal lives.

32
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:06.723
Flip the pictures over and match animals to their coverings.

33
00:02:08.023 --> 00:02:10.403
Look for legs, wings, fins, and tails.

34
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.943
Ask, "Does it live on land or in water, and how does it move?"

35
00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:18.743
Sort by covering, then by leg count, then by movement.

36
00:02:20.143 --> 00:02:21.643
Let your child pick a fourth rule.

37
00:02:21.643 --> 00:02:21.683
Flip the pictures over and match animals to your coverings.

38
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:22.503
Let your child pick a fourth rule.

39
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:25.117
A bat flies, and a penguin has feathers.

40
00:02:26.537 --> 00:02:30.097
Imagine your child sorts those two pictures by body covering.

41
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:35.617
Before you turn the cards over, predict whether the bat and penguin will go in the

42
00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:36.617
same group.

43
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.030
Turn the bat and penguin cards over.

44
00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.650
Ask, "Which one flies, and which one has feathers?"

45
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.690
Bats have fur, and penguins have feathers.

46
00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.490
Put them in different groups when you sort by covering.

47
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.790
The group depends on the feature you choose.

48
00:02:58.883 --> 00:03:02.683
Wrap and refrigerate the fish within two hours of taking it out.

49
00:03:03.903 --> 00:03:07.623
If the room is above ninety degrees Fahrenheit, you have one hour.

50
00:03:08.843 --> 00:03:10.923
If it has been out longer, throw it away.

51
00:03:12.223 --> 00:03:14.883
Wash hands with soap and water for twenty seconds.

52
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:18.483
Wash the tray and table with soap and water.
